  "reasoning": [
    "For q=4*sin(theta/2)^2, the solid angle differential is pi*dq. The unit falloff is 1 for q<=qinner and has a smoothstep transition whose normalized integral equals one half, yielding pi*(qinner+qouter)/2.",
    "The implementation computes that value with sine half angles, preserving small-angle precision and avoiding cancellation from 1-cos(theta).",
    "Output is assigned only after finite angle/range validation and positive finite area validation. Invalid and underflowing inputs preserve the output.",
    "VisualRuntime divides declared luminous flux times color by the same effective solid angle, validates finite float intensity, and sends the corresponding squared-chord boundaries to the shader.",
    "The independent theta-domain quadrature includes 2*pi*sin(theta), narrow and wide cones, and measures the integrated declared flux."
  ],
  "scope_boundary": "VisualRuntime and Deferred HLSL were reviewed at the recorded hashes. Subsequent seam-sampling changes are reviewed separately.",
